  "term": "ACTH",
  "definition": "ACTH, or adrenocorticotropic hormone, is a pituitary hormone that signals the adrenal cortex to release adrenal steroids, especially cortisone, as part of the body’s stress response. The packet describes recombinant corticotropin as a lab-made form that is identical or similar to human ACTH.",
